# Git branches — start from latest main

Every new feature branch must start from the current tip of `origin/main`
after fetching. Do not branch from a stale local `main`, another feature
branch, or an old commit.

## Required workflow

```bash
git fetch origin main
git switch -c <branch> origin/main
```

Use `git checkout -b <branch> origin/main` when `switch` is unavailable.

## Forbidden

- `git switch -c feature` while HEAD is behind `origin/main`
- `git switch -c feature main` without verifying `main` matches `origin/main`
- `git switch -c feature other-branch`

## Enforcement

- Cursor `.cursor/hooks/validate-branch-off-main.sh` blocks branch-create
  commands that do not start from `origin/main`
- Codex `.codex/hooks/validate-branch-off-main.sh` applies the same check on
  Bash `PreToolUse` (requires `features.codex_hooks = true` in
  `~/.codex/config.toml`)
- Both hooks call `script/branch_off_main_policy.py`
